   "error": null,
   "response_text": "Fixed! \ud83d\udc36\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/types.py`, `BoolParamType.convert()` did `norm = value.strip()` \u2014 it trimmed surrounding whitespace but never normalized case. The subsequent membership tests compared against all-lowercase literal sets (`{\"true\",\"t\",\"yes\",\"y\",\"on\",...}`), so anything with uppercase letters (`TRUE`, `Yes`, `Off`) fell straight through to the `fail(...)` call.\n\n**Fix:** one-character-level change \u2014 lowercase after stripping:\n\n```python\nnorm = value.strip().lower()\n```\n\nThat makes the spellings case-insensitive while `strip()` already handles the whitespace-ignoring part.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `--debug TRUE` / `Yes` / `Off` / ` on ` / ` 1 ` / `N` all convert correctly now.\n- Genuinely invalid input (`maybe`) still fails with `is not a valid boolean.`\n- Full test suite: `588 passed, 22 skipped, 1 xfailed` (no test files touched, only the library source).\n\nDONE",
